1	# Data Model: P-RF04 — Interactive chat with memory (RAG)
2	
3	Source: spec.md §Key Entities; requirements.md §§1 (RF04), 6.3, 8, 10, 13; `docs/input/backend/api/
4	openapi.yaml`'s `/chat/sessions*` schemas; `docs/input/backend/error-taxonomy.md`;
5	`docs/input/prototype/prototype-extract.md` §§2.2, 3, 4, 6. This is a new feature folder,
6	`lib/features/chat/`, depending on `core/network/*` (extended, R1/R8), `features/session/domain/repositories/
7	session_repository.dart` (unchanged, read-only reuse), and nothing from `entries/`/`records/` (chat never
8	touches the entries pipeline in this unit — FR-003/FR-014).
9	
10	## `ChatPersona` / `ChatSession` (`lib/features/chat/domain/entities/chat_session.dart`) — NEW
11	
12	```dart
13	enum ChatPersona { analitico, empatico, socratico }
14	
15	class ChatSession extends Equatable {
16	  const ChatSession({
17	    required this.id,
18	    required this.title,
19	    required this.personaSnapshot,
20	    required this.userMessageCount,
21	    required this.lastUserMessageAt,
22	    required this.createdAt,
23	    required this.updatedAt,
24	  });
25	
26	  final String id;
27	  final String title;
28	  final ChatPersona personaSnapshot;   // read-only here (FR-014) — never written back
29	  final int userMessageCount;
30	  final DateTime? lastUserMessageAt;   // nullable per schema; in practice always non-null once listed (spec.md Key Entities)
31	  final DateTime createdAt;
32	  final DateTime updatedAt;
33	
34	  @override
35	  List<Object?> get props =>
36	      [id, title, personaSnapshot, userMessageCount, lastUserMessageAt, createdAt, updatedAt];
37	}
38	```
39	
40	Every field above is `required` in both `chat.sessions.create`'s and `chat.sessions.list`'s response schema
41	(openapi.yaml) — none is optional to model, mirroring `Entry`'s own precedent (RF01 data-model.md).
42	
43	## `ChatRole` / `ChatMessageStatus` / `ChatMessage` (`lib/features/chat/domain/entities/chat_message.dart`) — NEW
44	
45	```dart
46	enum ChatRole { user, assistant }
47	enum ChatMessageStatus { streaming, complete, failed }
48	
49	class ChatMessage extends Equatable {
50	  const ChatMessage({
51	    required this.id,
52	    required this.sessionId,
53	    required this.role,
54	    required this.content,
55	    required this.seq,
56	    required this.status,
57	    required this.retryCount,
58	    required this.createdAt,
59	  });
60	
61	  final String id;           // `local-<timestamp>`-prefixed until reconciled (research.md R5)
62	  final String sessionId;
63	  final ChatRole role;
64	  final String content;      // grows incrementally while status == streaming (token deltas appended)
65	  final int seq;
66	  final ChatMessageStatus status;
67	  final int retryCount;
68	  final DateTime createdAt;
69	
70	  bool get isOptimistic => id.startsWith('local-');
71	
72	  @override
73	  List<Object?> get props => [id, sessionId, role, content, seq, status, retryCount, createdAt];
74	}
75	```
76	
77	Matches `chat-messages-list`'s response schema field-for-field. `seq` for an optimistic placeholder (R5) is
78	set to `previousMessage.seq + 1` (or `0` for the very first message of a brand-new session) purely so the
79	list's existing sort-by-`seq` ordering holds before the server's own `seq` is known; it is overwritten once
80	real data arrives via `message_created`/`done` (R2) — the server is always the final authority on ordering.
81	
82	**Status transitions** (FR-004):
83	
84	```
85	(message sent/retried)
86	     │
87	     ▼
88	 streaming ──(done event)──► complete
89	     │
90	     └──(error event, DioException, or connection drop)──► failed
91	```
92	
93	`complete` and `failed` are terminal for that specific turn; `failed` is the only state eligible for
94	`MessageRetryRequested`, which starts a **new** `streaming` message at the same list position (R10) rather
95	than mutating the failed one — `retryCount` increments on each such replacement, for the UI's own benefit
96	(not currently rendered anywhere, but captured since the server's response carries it).
97	
98	## `ChatSessionsPage` (`lib/features/chat/domain/entities/chat_sessions_page.dart`) — NEW
99	
100	```dart
101	class ChatSessionsPage extends Equatable {
102	  const ChatSessionsPage({required this.sessions, required this.nextCursor});
103	
104	  final List<ChatSession> sessions;   // ordered by lastUserMessageAt desc (FR-008; backend-ordered — see contracts/chat-repository.md)
105	  final String? nextCursor;           // meta.nextCursor verbatim; null = last page
106	
107	  @override
108	  List<Object?> get props => [sessions, nextCursor];
109	}
110	```
111	
112	Directly mirrors `EntriesPage` (RF01/RF07) — same shape, same "null `nextCursor` = last page" convention.
113	
114	## `ChatStreamEvent` (`lib/features/chat/domain/entities/chat_stream_event.dart`) — NEW
115	
116	```dart
117	sealed class ChatStreamEvent extends Equatable {
118	  const ChatStreamEvent();
119	}
120	
121	class MessageCreated extends ChatStreamEvent {
122	  const MessageCreated({required this.userMessageId, required this.assistantMessageId});
123	  final String userMessageId;
124	  final String assistantMessageId;
125	  @override List<Object?> get props => [userMessageId, assistantMessageId];
126	}
127	
128	class ContextReceived extends ChatStreamEvent {
129	  const ContextReceived();
130	  @override List<Object?> get props => [];
131	}
132	
133	class TokenReceived extends ChatStreamEvent {
134	  const TokenReceived(this.delta);
135	  final String delta;
136	  @override List<Object?> get props => [delta];
137	}
138	
139	class StreamDone extends ChatStreamEvent {
140	  const StreamDone({required this.assistantMessageId, required this.content, required this.createdAt});
141	  final String assistantMessageId;
142	  final String content;
143	  final DateTime createdAt;
144	  @override List<Object?> get props => [assistantMessageId, content, createdAt];
145	}
146	```
147	
148	No `ErrorEvent` variant — a business-level `error` SSE frame and a transport-level `DioException` both become
149	a `Left(Failure)` on the *same* `Stream<Either<Failure, ChatStreamEvent>>` (research.md R1/R2), so
150	`ChatBloc`/`ChatSessionsBloc` only ever need one failure-handling branch per stream, exactly like every other
151	`Either`-returning call in this codebase.
152	
153	## `ChatTitleDeriver` (`lib/features/chat/domain/entities/chat_title_deriver.dart`) — NEW
154	
155	```dart
156	class ChatTitleDeriver {
157	  const ChatTitleDeriver._();
158	
159	  static const _maxLength = 48;
160	
161	  /// Pure, total; never returns an empty string given a non-empty `firstMessageText`
162	  /// (research.md R6). No `package:flutter` import, no I/O.
163	  static String derive(String firstMessageText) {
164	    final collapsed = firstMessageText.replaceAll(RegExp(r'\s+'), ' ').trim();
165	    if (collapsed.length <= _maxLength) return collapsed;
166	    return '${collapsed.substring(0, _maxLength)}…';
167	  }
168	}
169	```
170	
171	## `ChatRepository` (`lib/features/chat/domain/repositories/chat_repository.dart`) — NEW
172	
173	```dart
174	abstract class ChatRepository {
175	  /// `POST /chat/sessions` (`chat-sessions-create`). Retries exactly once through
176	  /// `SessionRepository.refresh()` on `AuthExpiredFailure` (same shape as every other
177	  /// non-streaming call in this codebase).
178	  Future<Either<Failure, ChatSession>> createSession({required String title});
179	
180	  /// `GET /chat/sessions` (`chat-sessions-list`), ordered by `lastUserMessageAt` desc (FR-008).
181	  Future<Either<Failure, ChatSessionsPage>> listSessions({String? cursor, int? limit});
182	
183	  /// Every session returned by any successful [listSessions] call this process has made,
184	  /// backed by `ChatLocalCache` so it survives a restart (research.md R4) — the offline
185	  /// fallback `ChatSessionsBloc` reads when a fetch fails outright.
186	  List<ChatSession> get cachedSessions;
187	
188	  /// `GET /chat/sessions/:id/messages` (`chat-messages-list`), ordered by `seq`.
189	  Future<Either<Failure, List<ChatMessage>>> listMessages(String sessionId);
190	
191	  /// The last successfully-fetched message list for [sessionId], or `null` if this session's
192	  /// history has never been fetched while online (research.md R4/Clarification 3) — `null`
193	  /// is the signal `ChatBloc` uses to show the "standard no-connection state" instead of any
194	  /// content when selecting it while offline.
195	  List<ChatMessage>? cachedMessages(String sessionId);
196	
197	  /// Persists which conversation to resume on next app open (spec.md Assumptions).
198	  Future<void> setLastActiveSessionId(String? sessionId);
199	  Future<String?> get lastActiveSessionId;
200	
201	  /// `POST /chat/sessions/:id/messages` (`chat-messages-send`), SSE. Retries the whole call
202	  /// exactly once via `SessionRepository.refresh()` only if the very first emitted item is
203	  /// `AuthExpiredFailure` (research.md R3).
204	  Stream<Either<Failure, ChatStreamEvent>> sendMessage({
205	    required String sessionId,
206	    required String content,
207	  });
208	
209	  /// `POST /chat/sessions/:id/messages/:userMessageId/retry` (`chat-messages-retry`), SSE.
210	  /// Same retry-once-if-first-frame-fails shape as [sendMessage] (research.md R3).
211	  Stream<Either<Failure, ChatStreamEvent>> retryMessage({
212	    required String sessionId,
213	    required String userMessageId,
214	  });
215	}
216	```
217	
218	See `contracts/chat-repository.md` for `ChatRemoteDataSource`/`ChatRepositoryImpl`'s exact implementation and
219	the full SSE frame→event mapping.
220	
221	## `SseFrame` / `ApiClient.sseStream` (`lib/core/network/sse_frame.dart`, extends `api_client.dart`) — NEW, shared
222	
223	```dart
224	class SseFrame extends Equatable {
225	  const SseFrame({required this.event, required this.data});
226	  final String event;   // e.g. "message_created", "context", "token", "done", "error"
227	  final String data;    // raw JSON text, parsed by the caller (ChatRemoteDataSource) — ApiClient stays generic
228	  @override List<Object?> get props => [event, data];
229	}
230	```
231	
232	```dart
233	class ApiClient {
234	  // ...existing call()...
235	
236	  /// Generic SSE transport (research.md R1) — knows nothing about chat specifically. Never
237	  /// throws past this boundary, same guarantee as call(): a transport failure becomes the
238	  /// stream's one and only `Left(Failure)` item, then the stream closes.
239	  Stream<Either<Failure, SseFrame>> sseStream(
240	    String function, {
241	    required String method,
242	    Map<String, dynamic>? body,
243	    List<String>? pathSegments,
244	    AuthMode authMode = AuthMode.userSession,
245	  });
246	}
247	```
248	
249	## `ChatLocalCache` (`lib/features/chat/data/chat_local_cache.dart`) — NEW
250	
251	```dart
252	class ChatLocalCache {
253	  ChatLocalCache({FlutterSecureStorage? storage}) : _storage = storage ?? const FlutterSecureStorage();
254	  final FlutterSecureStorage _storage;
255	
256	  static const _sessionsKey = 'chatSessionsLocalCache';
257	  static const _messagesKey = 'chatMessagesLocalCache';
258	  static const _lastActiveKey = 'chatLastActiveSessionId';
259	
260	  Future<List<ChatSession>> readSessions();
261	  Future<void> writeSessions(List<ChatSession> sessions);        // upsert-by-id merge, like EntriesLocalCache
262	
263	  Future<Map<String, List<ChatMessage>>> readAllMessages();
264	  Future<void> writeMessagesForSession(String sessionId, List<ChatMessage> messages);  // replace-whole-list
265	
266	  Future<String?> readLastActiveSessionId();
267	  Future<void> writeLastActiveSessionId(String? sessionId);
268	}
269	```
270	
271	On-disk JSON shapes (research.md R4):
272	
273	```jsonc
274	// key: chatSessionsLocalCache
275	[{"id": "...", "title": "...", "personaSnapshot": "analitico", "userMessageCount": 3,
276	  "lastUserMessageAt": "2026-10-19T12:00:00.000Z", "createdAt": "...", "updatedAt": "..."}, ...]
277	
278	// key: chatMessagesLocalCache
279	{"<sessionId>": [{"id": "...", "sessionId": "...", "role": "user", "content": "...",
280	                  "seq": 0, "status": "complete", "retryCount": 0, "createdAt": "..."}, ...], ...}
281	
282	// key: chatLastActiveSessionId
283	"<sessionId>"   // a bare JSON string, or the key is simply absent when no session exists yet
284	```
285	
286	## `ChatRepositoryImpl` (`lib/features/chat/data/chat_repository_impl.dart`) — NEW
287	
288	Wraps `ChatRemoteDataSource` + `ChatLocalCache` + `SessionRepository` (for the silent-refresh retry,
289	research.md R3) — same constructor shape as `EntriesRepositoryImpl`. `createSession`/`listSessions`/
290	`listMessages` each go through the existing `_retryAfterSilentRefresh` pattern verbatim; `sendMessage`/
291	`retryMessage` apply R3's "only if the first frame fails" variant. Every successful `listSessions`/
292	`listMessages` result is written through to `ChatLocalCache` before being returned (mirroring
293	`EntriesRepositoryImpl._cacheAndPersist`).
294	
295	## `ChatEvent` / `ChatState` (`lib/features/chat/presentation/bloc/`) — NEW
296	
297	| Event | When |
298	|---|---|
299	| `ChatStarted` | Dispatched once by `app_router.dart`'s `/home` route builder, right after `ChatBloc` is constructed — resumes `lastActiveSessionId`, or shows the empty state if none exists. |
300	| `ConversationSelected(String sessionId)` | Tapping a past conversation in the side menu (dispatched by `AppDrawer` to the shared `ChatBloc`, research.md R7). |
301	| `NewConversationRequested` | Tapping "Novo Chat" (same dispatch path). Drops `sessionId`/`messages`, shows the empty, ready-to-send state — no repository call (FR-010's "MUST NOT by itself create a session"). |
302	| `MessageSubmitted(String text)` | The composer's send tap. |
303	| `MessageRetryRequested(String userMessageId)` | Tapping a `failed` message bubble. |
304	| `_ConnectivityChanged(bool isOnline)` *(internal)* | Fired by the `ConnectivityChecker.onConnectivityChanged` subscription `ChatBloc` opens in its constructor (research.md R8). |
305	
306	```dart
307	sealed class ChatState extends Equatable { const ChatState(); }
308	
309	class ChatLoading extends ChatState { const ChatLoading(); }   // only while resuming lastActiveSessionId on ChatStarted
310	
311	/// Everything else — an existing conversation, the empty "Novo Chat" state, or an outright
312	/// load failure with nothing cached to fall back to, are all one state shape so the screen
313	/// never has to discard/rebuild its `Scaffold`/`AppBar` switching between them.
314	class ChatReady extends ChatState {
315	  const ChatReady({
316	    required this.sessionId,            // null = empty conversation, no session created yet (FR-010)
317	    required this.messages,             // [] for an empty conversation
318	    required this.isOffline,
319	    required this.awaitingResponse,     // research.md R9 — gates the composer, true during a send/retry turn
320	    this.loadFailure,                   // set only when selecting an existing session's history failed outright
321	                                         // AND nothing is cached for it (Clarification 3's no-content edge case)
322	  });
323	
324	  final String? sessionId;
325	  final List<ChatMessage> messages;
326	  final bool isOffline;
327	  final bool awaitingResponse;
328	  final Failure? loadFailure;
329	
330	  bool get canSend => !isOffline && !awaitingResponse && loadFailure == null;
331	
332	  @override
333	  List<Object?> get props => [sessionId, messages, isOffline, awaitingResponse, loadFailure];
334	}
335	```
336	
337	`Stream<void> get reauthRequired` on `ChatBloc` — same one-shot-side-effect shape as `RecordsBloc`'s own
338	(research.md R3/R7; consumed by `HomeChatShellPage`, not `ChatBloc` itself).
339	
340	See `contracts/chat-bloc.md` for the full handler-by-handler sequencing (lazy session creation, the
341	optimistic-placeholder append, `emit.forEach` over the SSE stream, retry's position-matching).
342	
343	## `ChatSessionsEvent` / `ChatSessionsState` (`lib/features/chat/presentation/bloc/`) — NEW
344	
345	Directly mirrors `RecordsEvent`/`RecordsState`'s own shape (RF07), narrowed to one bounded concern:
346	
347	| Event | When |
348	|---|---|
349	| `SessionsStarted` | Dispatched once when `ChatSessionsBloc` is constructed (the drawer's very first open). |
350	| `SessionsRefreshRequested` | `Scaffold.onDrawerChanged(true)` on every subsequent open (research.md R7) — refetches page 1, keeps any already-loaded further pages' sessions merged in by id. |
351	| `SessionsNextPageRequested` | Scroll-to-bottom of the "CONVERSAS" section (FR-008). |
352	| `SessionsPageLoadRetried` | The inline retry affordance on a failed page-list fetch. |
353	
354	```dart
355	sealed class ChatSessionsState extends Equatable { const ChatSessionsState(); }
356	class ChatSessionsLoading extends ChatSessionsState { const ChatSessionsLoading(); }
357	class ChatSessionsLoadFailure extends ChatSessionsState {
358	  const ChatSessionsLoadFailure(this.failure);
359	  final Failure failure;
360	  @override List<Object?> get props => [failure];
361	}
362	class ChatSessionsLoaded extends ChatSessionsState {
363	  const ChatSessionsLoaded({
364	    required this.sessions,
365	    required this.nextCursor,
366	    required this.isLoadingMore,
367	    this.pageLoadFailure,
368	  });
369	  final List<ChatSession> sessions;
370	  final String? nextCursor;
371	  final bool isLoadingMore;
372	  final Failure? pageLoadFailure;
373	  bool get hasReachedEnd => nextCursor == null;
374	  @override List<Object?> get props => [sessions, nextCursor, isLoadingMore, pageLoadFailure];
375	}
376	```
377	
378	`Stream<void> get reauthRequired` here too — independent of `ChatBloc`'s own (two separate
379	`StreamController`s; `AppDrawer` listens to both and forwards each to the shared, app-wide `SessionBloc`).
380	
381	## Widgets (`lib/features/chat/presentation/`) — new; `home/` — extended in place
382	
383	- `lib/features/home/presentation/pages/home_chat_shell_page.dart` — **extended**. Wraps its `Scaffold` body
384	  with `BlocBuilder<ChatBloc, ChatState>`; the previously-inert `_ComposerBar` becomes `ChatComposer`
385	  (enabled per `ChatReady.canSend`); `Scaffold.onDrawerChanged` added, forwarding to `ChatSessionsBloc`
386	  (research.md R7). `ChatBloc`/`ChatSessionsBloc` are provided by the route builder in `app_router.dart`
387	  (`MultiBlocProvider`, replacing the current bare `const HomeChatShellPage()`), not inside this widget, same
388	  placement RF07 already uses for `RecordsBloc` on `AppRoutes.records`.
389	- `lib/features/home/presentation/widgets/app_drawer.dart` — **extended**, becomes a `StatefulWidget`. Adds
390	  the "CONVERSAS" section (`BlocBuilder<ChatSessionsBloc, ChatSessionsState>` + a `ListView`'s own
391	  `ScrollController`, same scroll-to-bottom-triggers-next-page shape `RecordsPage` already uses) above the
392	  existing "Meus Registros"/"Configurações" items, and a "Novo Chat" `ListTile` dispatching
393	  `NewConversationRequested` to `ChatBloc`. Each session row dispatches `ConversationSelected(session.id)` and
394	  closes the drawer.
395	- `lib/features/chat/presentation/widgets/chat_message_bubble.dart` — **NEW**. One widget, branching on
396	  `ChatMessage.role`/`status` (user vs. assistant bubble shape; `streaming` pulsing-cursor vs. `complete`
397	  timestamp vs. `failed` red "Falha ao gerar resposta — toque para tentar novamente" in place of the
398	  timestamp, tappable only when `failed`).
399	- `lib/features/chat/presentation/widgets/chat_composer.dart` — **NEW**, replaces `_ComposerBar`. Owns its own
400	  `TextEditingController` (never part of `ChatState` — research.md's own "composer text is local" choice,
401	  consistent with nothing being lost on any failure since it's simply never cleared except on a successful
402	  dispatch), `maxLength: 8000` (research.md R12), disabled per `ChatReady.canSend`.
403	- `lib/features/chat/presentation/widgets/chat_offline_banner.dart` — **NEW**. "Sem conexão — histórico
404	  disponível, novas mensagens bloqueadas" (prototype-extract.md §2.2), shown whenever `ChatReady.isOffline`.
405	
406	**Token reuse** (prototype-extract.md §§3, 6 — no new token, Principle IV):
407	
408	| Element | Token |
409	|---|---|
410	| User bubble | `DesignTokens.colorChatBubbleUser`, `radiusMd`, straight bottom-right corner |
411	| Assistant bubble | `DesignTokens.colorSurfaceElevated` + `elevation1`, `radiusMd`, straight bottom-left corner |
412	| Streaming cursor / failure text | `colorTextPrimary` (streaming) / `colorError` (failure), `textBodyMd` |
413	| Offline banner | `colorInfoOffline` background, `colorOnPrimary`-equivalent light text |
414	| Side menu section label ("CONVERSAS") | `textLabelMd` + `colorTextSecondary`, same as `AppDrawer`'s existing item styling |
415	| Composer send icon (enabled/disabled) | `colorPrimary` / `colorTextSecondary` — same pair `home_chat_shell_page.dart` already uses today |
416	
417	## DI (`lib/core/di/service_locator.dart`) — additions
418	
419	```dart
420	// Chat (P-RF04)
421	getIt.registerLazySingleton<ChatLocalCache>(ChatLocalCache.new);
422	getIt.registerLazySingleton<ChatRemoteDataSource>(() => ChatRemoteDataSource(getIt<ApiClient>()));
423	getIt.registerLazySingleton<ChatRepository>(() => ChatRepositoryImpl(
424	  getIt<ChatRemoteDataSource>(),
425	  sessionRepository: getIt<SessionRepository>(),
426	  localCache: getIt<ChatLocalCache>(),
427	));
428	getIt.registerFactory<ChatBloc>(() => ChatBloc(
429	  chatRepository: getIt<ChatRepository>(),
430	  connectivityChecker: getIt<ConnectivityChecker>(),
431	));
432	getIt.registerFactory<ChatSessionsBloc>(() => ChatSessionsBloc(chatRepository: getIt<ChatRepository>()));
433	```
434	
435	`ConnectivityChecker` is already registered (RF01) — only its own class gains `onConnectivityChanged`
436	(research.md R8), no new registration.
437	
438	## Routing (`lib/core/routing/app_router.dart`) — changed in place
439	
440	```dart
441	GoRoute(
442	  path: AppRoutes.home,
443	  builder: (context, state) => MultiBlocProvider(
444	    providers: [
445	      BlocProvider<ChatBloc>(create: (_) => getIt<ChatBloc>()..add(const ChatStarted())),
446	      BlocProvider<ChatSessionsBloc>(create: (_) => getIt<ChatSessionsBloc>()),
447	    ],
448	    child: const HomeChatShellPage(),
449	  ),
450	),
451	```
452	
453	`AppRoutes.home` itself is unchanged (`'/home'`, no parameter — research.md R7).
